# unit — module constants whose types are SPELLED in C, not just held behind a runtime
# pointer. A tuple and an optional each need a typedef in EVERY unit that declares the
# global — including this one, which never lowers the values: only the entry unit assigns
# constants. `pub SPAN := (1, 2)` reached cc as `unknown type name
# 'zgt_tup_int64_t_int64_t'` on this module's own unit, because the typedef was only ever
# registered where a value was lowered. A module constant is the one declaration site
# outside the c_decl_types walk — its global is rendered after the on-demand typedef
# stream, so c_const_globals registers what it spells at the moment it spells it.

# SPAN is a tuple constant, its type INFERRED from the value.
pub SPAN := (1, 2)

# CAP is an optional constant, its type WRITTEN — the value alone would say nil.
pub CAP: int? = nil
